    # email: FILL IN
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"

abstract: >-
  CompLB3D is a three-dimensional pore-scale reactive transport model. It
  couples lattice-Boltzmann flow and solute transport to microbial metabolism,
  aqueous speciation, and mineral precipitation and dissolution that change the
  pore geometry as the simulation runs. Metabolism is chosen per organism:
  hand-written kinetics, flux balance analysis through GLPK or COBRApy, or a
  trained surrogate neural network. It extends the two-dimensional CompLaB model
  and adds an equilibrium chemistry solver, an abiotic kinetics path, and
  mineral dissolution.

repository-code: "https://github.com/shahram444/CompLB3D-lattice-Boltzmann-FBA-surrogate-COBRApy-GLPK"
